          }
        ],
        "text": "(The boy cries.)",
        "notes": [
          "Restores the source-visible opening `(பையன் அழுதல்)`. The historical scene-29 copy of this action was removed; it belongs to canonical scene 30."
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "tirumbippaar-en-s030-u002",
        "kind": "stage-direction",
        "speakerLabel": null,
        "sourceRecordId": null,
        "sourceOccurrenceId": null,
        "pageProvenance": [
          {
            "pdfPage": 36,
            "printedPage": 28
          }
        ],
        "text": "(Bama's father, Gunarathnam, is sorrowfully telling Poomalai about his daughter.)",
        "notes": []
      },
      {
        "id": "tirumbippaar-en-s030-u003",
        "kind": "dialogue",
        "speakerLabel": "குணரத்னம்",
        "sourceRecordId": "tirumbippaar-s030-d001",
        "sourceOccurrenceId": null,
        "pageProvenance": [
          {
            "pdfPage": 36,
            "printedPage": 28
          }
        ],
        "text": "Was it only she who went? She mortgaged the house and went off with the thousand rupees' worth of jewellery I'd had made too!",
        "notes": []
      },
      {
        "id": "tirumbippaar-en-s030-u004",
        "kind": "dialogue",
        "speakerLabel": "பூமாலை",
        "sourceRecordId": "tirumbippaar-s030-d002",
        "sourceOccurrenceId": null,
        "pageProvenance": [
          {
            "pdfPage": 36,
            "printedPage": 28
          }
        ],
        "text": "It's only a thousand rupees' worth of jewellery, isn't it? Here.... (Removing her own ornaments and handing them over) Keep these. (She gives them.)",
        "notes": []
      },
      {
        "id": "tirumbippaar-en-s030-u005",
        "kind": "dialogue",
        "speakerLabel": "குணரத்னம்",
        "sourceRecordId": "tirumbippaar-s030-d003",
        "sourceOccurrenceId": null,
        "pageProvenance": [
          {
            "pdfPage": 36,
            "printedPage": 28
          }
        ],
        "text": "(Taking them) Why? Whom am I going to adorn with these and admire? You keep them yourself. (Throwing them down) Those who betrayed me will come to ruin!...",
        "notes": []
      },
      {
        "id": "tirumbippaar-en-s030-u006",
        "kind": "stage-direction",
        "speakerLabel": null,
        "sourceRecordId": null,
        "sourceOccurrenceId": null,
        "pageProvenance": [
          {
            "pdfPage": 37,
            "printedPage": 29
          }
        ],
        "text": "(He leaves. Poomalai sits wearily on the sofa. Paranthaman comes in and sees the jewellery lying on the floor.)",
        "notes": []
      },
      {
        "id": "tirumbippaar-en-s030-u007",
        "kind": "dialogue",
        "speakerLabel": "பரந்தாமன்",
        "sourceRecordId": "tirumbippaar-s030-d004",
        "sourceOccurrenceId": null,
        "pageProvenance": [
          {
            "pdfPage": 37,
            "printedPage": 29
          }
        ],
        "text": "Akka, where did this jewellery come from?",
        "notes": []
      },
      {
        "id": "tirumbippaar-en-s030-u008",
        "kind": "stage-direction",
        "speakerLabel": null,
        "sourceRecordId": null,
        "sourceOccurrenceId": null,
        "pageProvenance": [
          {
            "pdfPage": 37,
            "printedPage": 29
          }
        ],
        "text": "(Poomalai is silent.)",
        "notes": []
      },
      {
        "id": "tirumbippaar-en-s030-u009",
        "kind": "dialogue",
        "speakerLabel": "பரந்தாமன்",
        "sourceRecordId": "tirumbippaar-s030-d005",
        "sourceOccurrenceId": null,
        "pageProvenance": [
          {
            "pdfPage": 37,
            "printedPage": 29
          }
        ],
        "text": "Why is it lying down here like this? (He picks it up.) These are all gold ornaments, aren't they?",
        "notes": []
      },
      {
        "id": "tirumbippaar-en-s030-u010",
        "kind": "dialogue",
        "speakerLabel": "பூமாலை",
        "sourceRecordId": "tirumbippaar-s030-d006",
        "sourceOccurrenceId": null,
        "pageProvenance": [
          {
            "pdfPage": 37,
            "printedPage": 29
          }
        ],
        "text": "No. The smile of betrayal!",
        "notes": [
          "The source makes a wordplay between `பொன்னகை` (gold ornament) and `புன்னகை` (smile); the English preserves the semantic turn, though not the Tamil sound-play."
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "tirumbippaar-en-s030-u011",
        "kind": "dialogue",
        "speakerLabel": "பரந்தாமன்",
        "sourceRecordId": "tirumbippaar-s030-d007",
        "sourceOccurrenceId": null,
        "pageProvenance": [
          {
            "pdfPage": 37,
            "printedPage": 29
          }
        ],
        "text": "(As if he does not understand) What's this! What's the matter, akka?",
        "notes": []
      },
      {
        "id": "tirumbippaar-en-s030-u012",
        "kind": "dialogue",
        "speakerLabel": "பூமாலை",
        "sourceRecordId": "tirumbippaar-s030-d008",
        "sourceOccurrenceId": null,
        "pageProvenance": [
          {
            "pdfPage": 37,
            "printedPage": 29
          }
        ],
        "text": "A tiger cannot live long in a deerskin, Paranthama! A hunter will come to hunt it too. People do not leave alive those who toy with the women of the town!... Remember that!",
        "notes": []
      },
      {
        "id": "tirumbippaar-en-s030-u013",
        "kind": "dialogue",
        "speakerLabel": "பரந்தாமன்",
        "sourceRecordId": "tirumbippaar-s030-d009",
        "sourceOccurrenceId": null,
        "pageProvenance": [
          {
            "pdfPage": 37,
            "printedPage": 29
          }
        ],
        "text": "Every time I come home, is it this same lament? Looks as though a man can't live in peace at all!",
        "notes": []
      },
      {
        "id": "tirumbippaar-en-s030-u014",
        "kind": "dialogue",
        "speakerLabel": "பூமாலை",
        "sourceRecordId": "tirumbippaar-s030-d010",
        "sourceOccurrenceId": null,
        "pageProvenance": [
          {
            "pdfPage": 37,
            "printedPage": 29
          }
        ],
        "text": "A man must not live only for himself. He must let others live too!",
        "notes": []
      },
      {
        "id": "tirumbippaar-en-s030-u015",
        "kind": "dialogue",
        "speakerLabel": "பரந்தாமன்",
        "sourceRecordId": "tirumbippaar-s030-d011",
        "sourceOccurrenceId": null,
        "pageProvenance": [
          {
            "pdfPage": 37,
            "printedPage": 29
          }
        ],
        "text": "All right, enough, enough. I suppose I should put on saffron robes and disappear somewhere.",
        "notes": []
      },
      {
        "id": "tirumbippaar-en-s030-u016",
        "kind": "dialogue",
        "speakerLabel": "பூமாலை",
        "sourceRecordId": "tirumbippaar-s030-d012",
        "sourceOccurrenceId": null,
        "pageProvenance": [
          {
            "pdfPage": 37,
            "printedPage": 29
          }
        ],
        "text": "Why! Do you think you can deceive people easily behind that screen? Madman who has regarded womankind as a swarm of worms writhing in the earth! Where did Bama go? Tell me. Where did you leave her to suffer? What became of that poor young girl who came to play on a volcano? Tell me! Won't you tell me, sinner! Where is Bama?",
        "notes": []
      },
      {
        "id": "tirumbippaar-en-s030-u017",
        "kind": "dialogue",
        "speakerLabel": "பரந்தாமன்",
        "sourceRecordId": "tirumbippaar-s030-d013",
        "sourceOccurrenceId": null,
        "pageProvenance": [
          {
            "pdfPage": 37,
            "printedPage": 29
          }
        ],
        "text": "Go and look for her in the other world!",
        "notes": []
      },
      {
        "id": "tirumbippaar-en-s030-u018",
        "kind": "stage-direction",
        "speakerLabel": null,
        "sourceRecordId": null,
        "sourceOccurrenceId": null,
        "pageProvenance": [
          {
            "pdfPage": 37,
            "printedPage": 29
          }
        ],
        "text": "(He leaves.)",
        "notes": []
      },
      {
        "id": "tirumbippaar-en-s030-u019",
        "kind": "dialogue",
        "speakerLabel": "பூமாலை",
        "sourceRecordId": "tirumbippaar-s030-d014",
        "sourceOccurrenceId": null,
        "pageProvenance": [
          {
            "pdfPage": 38,
            "printedPage": 30
          }
        ],
        "text": "(Tears welling) Ah! Amma! Appa! It seems I will not be able to keep the promise I gave you!",
        "notes": []
      }
    ]
  }
}
